  "title": "China's regulators convene banks to widen stock support tools",
  "summary": "The People's Bank of China, the securities regulator and the banking regulator were due to meet major banks on Monday to study improvements to a relending facility that finances share buybacks and stake purchases, according to mainland media reports. The Shanghai Composite closed at 3,599.00 on Friday, down 6.3% in October and below 3,600 for the first time this year, while the Shenzhen Component fell 15.9% over the month.",
